% NOTE: Autogenerated stub. Adjust predicates/logic to your KB.
% technique_id: T1546.002
% technique_name: Screensaver
% domain: enterprise
% tactic(s): persistence;privilege-escalation
% platforms: Windows
% url: https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1546/002
% is_subtechnique: yes
% stix_id: attack-pattern--ce4b7013-640e-48a9-b501-d0025a95f4bf
% description: Adversaries may establish persistence by executing malicious content triggered by user inactivity. Screensavers are programs that execute after a configurable time of user inactivity and consist of Portable Executable (PE) files with a .scr file extension.(Citation: Wikipedia Screensaver) The Windows screensaver application scrnsave.scr is located in <code>C:\Windows\System32\</code>, and <code>C:\Windows\sysWOW64\</code>  on 64-bit Windows systems, along with screensavers included with base Windows installations.  The following screensaver settings are stored in the Registry (<code>HKCU\Control Panel\Desktop\</code>) and could be manipulated to achieve persistence:  * <code>SCRNSAVE.exe</code> - set to malicious PE path * <code>ScreenSaveActive</code> - set to '1' to enable the screensaver * <code>ScreenSaverIsSecure</code> - set to '0' to not require a password to unlock * <code>ScreenSaveTimeout</code> - sets user inactivity timeout before screensaver is executed  Adversaries can use screensaver settings to maintain persistence by setting the screensaver to run malware after a certain timeframe of user inactivity.(Citation: ESET Gazer Aug 2017)
% generated_by: notebook_generate_rules

% ---- RULE LLM START (minimal) ----
    persistence(Host, screensaver) :-
        attacker_at(net),
        connects(net, Host, _Port),
        setting(Host, 'HKCU\\Control Panel\\Desktop\\SCRNSAVE.exe', MaliciousPEPath),
        setting(Host, 'HKCU\\Control Panel\\Desktop\\ScreenSaveActive', '1'),
        setting(Host, 'HKCU\\Control Panel\\Desktop\\ScreenSaverIsSecure', '0'),
        setting(Host, 'HKCU\\Control Panel\\Desktop\\ScreenSaveTimeout', _Timeout),
        malicious_app_installed(Host, MaliciousPEPath).

    compromise(Host, user) :-
        persistence(Host, screensaver).
% ---- RULE LLM END ----
